1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,002
This is the first screen a relationship manager sees. Not a dashboard — a ranked list of who to call.

2
00:00:10,002 --> 00:00:22,005
Three conversations worth having this week. Seven clients with nothing to raise — checked, and clean. Every count is derived, never typed.

3
00:00:22,005 --> 00:00:32,008
Each row carries one sentence that can be defended, ordered by urgency rather than portfolio size.

4
00:00:32,008 --> 00:00:44,011
Abdullah Al-Mansoori. Forty-nine, Balanced Growth, thirty-two point two million. He asked a question in August that still has no answer.

5
00:00:44,011 --> 00:00:56,013
His objective, on file since two thousand and fourteen: build wealth outside the Gulf, and outside shipping. Forty-two per cent of the portfolio is energy and industrials.

6
00:00:56,013 --> 00:01:08,014
On any allocation report these are four separate things — two funds, a stock, a structured product. It looks diversified.

7
00:01:08,014 --> 00:01:20,017
Look through the note, and they are one bet. It references two names already held outright.

8
00:01:20,017 --> 00:01:30,019
Four positions. Forty-two point one per cent. One concentrated bet — read from a single record.

9
00:01:30,019 --> 00:01:40,022
Now the mandate. Every band, against what the portfolio actually holds.

10
00:01:40,022 --> 00:01:53,025
Every band is respected. Nothing in this bank's monitoring would raise anything here — and it is still forty-two per cent one bet. That gap is the product.

11
00:01:53,025 --> 00:02:05,027
He asked what happens if the Strait reopens. Two and a half million comes off the portfolio, and his charter rates fall the same week.

12
00:02:05,027 --> 00:02:17,027
The opening line, drafted from the findings above. Every figure in it was computed before the sentence was written.

13
00:02:17,027 --> 00:02:30,000
Every sentence traces to a row — the file, the identifiers, the values. A finding without evidence is not shown.
